{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":45,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.prescribed_not_minimiser_A5_conventionC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.prescribed_not_minimiser_A5_conventionC","kind":"theorem","line":471,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L471-L486","doc":"**The refutation under convention C**, in the shape this file\noriginally carried: `q = t²` with `t > 1`, and `hU` the polynomial sign\ncondition `0 ≤ Ã - B̃t¹²` (satisfied at the substrate anchor\n`t = √q₀`, where it evaluates to `≈ 0.604`; the exact window is\n`q < 1.13699…`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sortedV1_zC_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sortedV1_zC_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":462,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L462-L469","doc":"The sign hypothesis `hU` under convention C, in the committed\npolynomial form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sortedV1_zC_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sortedV1_zC_eq","kind":"theorem","line":447,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L447-L460","doc":"Under convention C at `q = t²`, the sorted position-`1` readout takes\nthe committed polynomial form `(Ã - B̃t¹²)/(K t⁶)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.K_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.K_pos","kind":"theorem","line":443,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L443-L445","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.K","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.K","kind":"def","line":440,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L440-L441","doc":"`K t = (t²+1)(t⁴+1)` — their common denominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.Bnum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.Bnum","kind":"def","line":436,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L436-L438","doc":"`B̃ = t⁶ + t⁴ - t³` — the cleared numerator of `c₋` under convention C\nat `q = t²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.Anum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.Anum","kind":"def","line":432,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L432-L434","doc":"`Ã = t³ + t² + 1` — the cleared numerator of `c₊` under convention C at\n`q = t²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cMinus_zC_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cMinus_zC_pos","kind":"theorem","line":429,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L429-L430","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cPlus_zC_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cPlus_zC_pos","kind":"theorem","line":424,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L424-L427","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.zC_lt_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.zC_lt_self","kind":"theorem","line":413,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L413-L422","doc":"`z_C < q` for `q > 1`: convention C also lies below `λ₊ = q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.zC_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.zC_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L409-L411","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.zC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.zC","kind":"def","line":405,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L405-L407","doc":"Convention C, `z = √q/(q+1)`: excised by the owner ruling of\n2026-08-15, retained here only as a cross-check. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.prescribed_not_minimiser_A5_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.prescribed_not_minimiser_A5_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":385,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L385-L396","doc":"**The refutation under the canonical convention D**, with every\nhypothesis discharged except the `q`-range.  `1 < q ≤ 6/5` contains the\nsubstrate anchor `q₀ ≈ 1.10998`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sharedV3_zD_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sharedV3_zD_pos","kind":"theorem","line":372,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L372-L383","doc":"Under convention D the shared position-`3` readout collapses to\n`1/(q(q² + 1)) > 0` — in particular it is never zero, so the shared tail\nnever degenerates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sharedV2_zD_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sharedV2_zD_pos","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L360-L370","doc":"Under convention D the shared position-`2` readout is\n`(q⁴ + 1)/(q²(q² + 1)) > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sortedV1_zD_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sortedV1_zD_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L347-L358","doc":"The sign hypothesis `hU`, discharged for convention D on `1 < q ≤ 6/5`\n— an interval that contains the substrate anchor `q₀ ≈ 1.10998` (the exact\nwindow is `q < 1.21060…`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sortedV1_zD_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sortedV1_zD_eq","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L336-L345","doc":"Under convention D the sorted position-`1` readout is\n`(q⁴ + 1 - q⁶)/(q³(q² + 1))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cMinus_zD_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cMinus_zD_pos","kind":"theorem","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L333-L334","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cPlus_zD_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cPlus_zD_pos","kind":"theorem","line":330,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L330-L331","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.zD_lt_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.zD_lt_self","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L323-L328","doc":"`q - z_D = q/(q² + 1) > 0`: convention D lies below `λ₊ = q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.zD_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.zD_pos","kind":"theorem","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L320-L321","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.zD","kind":"def","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L317-L318","doc":"Convention D, `z = q³/(q²+1)`: the canonical Markov parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.prescribed_not_minimiser_A5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.prescribed_not_minimiser_A5","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L301-L313","doc":"**The `A ≥ 4` clause of `prop:ground-state-ordering` is false.**  The\nstatement \"the prescribed arrangement minimises `Φ_q`\" fails at\n`A = 5, Z = 1, N = 4`: there is a strictly better arrangement (the sorted\none), so no minimality claim about the prescribed arrangement can hold.\nStated for an arbitrary Markov parameter whose readout weights are\npositive — in particular for convention D, the canonical one. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:ground-state-ordering","label":"prop:ground-state-ordering","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ground-state-ordering.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sorted_lt_prescribed_A5_full","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sorted_lt_prescribed_A5_full","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L287-L299","doc":"**`Φ_q` form of the refutation.**  Multiplying in the two shared\npositions, the *full* four-position readout product of the sorted\narrangement `p n n n n` is strictly smaller in absolute value than that of\nthe prescribed `n p n n n`.  Taking `Real.log` of both sides, this is\n`Φ_q(p n n n n) < Φ_q(n p n n n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sorted_lt_prescribed_A5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sorted_lt_prescribed_A5","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L250-L285","doc":"**The `A ≥ 4` clause of `prop:ground-state-ordering` is FALSE.**\n\nAt `A = 5`, `Z = 1`, `N = 4` the arrangement prescribed by rules (i)+(ii)\nis `n p n n n`.  For every `q > 1`, every Markov parameter `z` whose two\nreadout weights are positive, and under the sign hypothesis `hU` on the\nsorted readout, the **sorted** arrangement `p n n n n` — which the\nproposition reserves for `A ≤ 3` — has a strictly smaller readout product\nat the two positions where the arrangements differ:\n\n    |V̂₀ V̂₁| (sorted)  <  |V̂₀ V̂₁| (prescribed).\n\nSince positions `2, 3` agree, this is `Φ_q(p n n n n) < Φ_q(n p n n n)`:\nrules (i)+(ii) do **not** select the `Φ_q` minimiser at `A = 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.readout_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.readout_gap","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L230-L246","doc":"**The gap identity.**  The two arrangements' differing readout products\ndiffer by an expression in which `z` survives only inside the product\n`c₊c₋`:\n\n    V̂₀V̂₁(prescribed) - V̂₀V̂₁(sorted) = 2·c₊·c₋·c⁴·(q⁶ - 1)/q³.\n\nFor `q > 1` the last two factors are positive, so the sign of the gap is\nthe sign of `c₊c₋`, which `weight_prod` computes.  It degenerates to\nequality exactly at `q = 1`, where the deformation switches off. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sortedV0_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sortedV0_eq","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L219-L226","doc":"The `μ₊ = μ₋` position is `z`-free: it collapses to `c⁴` by\n`cPlus_add_cMinus`, whatever the Markov parameter is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sharedV3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sharedV3","kind":"def","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L215-L217","doc":"Position `3` of **both** arrangements: a neutron with one neutron after\nit (`μ₊ = q⁻¹`, `μ₋ = -q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sharedV2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sharedV2","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L210-L213","doc":"Position `2` of **both** arrangements: a neutron with two neutrons\nafter it (`μ₊ = q⁻²`, `μ₋ = (-q)² = q²`).  Identical in the two\narrangements, because at positions `2, 3` both suffixes are all-neutron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.prescribedV1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.prescribedV1","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L205-L208","doc":"The readout at position `1` of `n p n n n`: a proton with three\nneutrons after it, so `μ₊ = c³` and `μ₋ = (-c)³ = -c³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.prescribedV0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.prescribedV0","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L199-L203","doc":"The readout at position `0` of the **prescribed** arrangement\n`n p n n n` (rules (i)+(ii) at `Z = 1`, `N = 4`): a neutron with one proton\nand three neutrons after it, so `μ₊ = c·q⁻³`, `μ₋ = (-c)(-q)³ = c·q³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sortedV1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sortedV1","kind":"def","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L195-L197","doc":"The readout at position `1` of `p n n n n`: a neutron with three\nneutrons after it, so `μ₊ = q⁻³` and `μ₋ = (-q)³ = -q³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sortedV0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.sortedV0","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L190-L193","doc":"The readout at position `0` of the **sorted** arrangement `p n n n n`:\na proton whose whole suffix is neutrons, so all four crossings are mixed\n(`d = -h/2`), giving `μ₊ = μ₋ = c⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cMinus_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cMinus_pos","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L184-L186","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cPlus_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cPlus_pos","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L180-L182","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.weight_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.weight_prod","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L168-L178","doc":"The weight product, cleared: `4c₊c₋ = 4q(q - z)(qz + 1)/(q² + 1)²`.\nIts sign is that of `(q - z)(qz + 1)`, so **both weights are positive\nexactly when `-q⁻¹ < z < q`** — the Markov parameter strictly between the\ntwo eigenvalues `λ₋ = -q⁻¹` and `λ₊ = q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cPlus_add_cMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cPlus_add_cMinus","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L157-L166","doc":"**The two weights sum to `1`, identically in `z`.**  This is the whole\nreason the refutation is convention-independent: `z` is an affine parameter\non a partition of unity, so the `μ₊ = μ₋` positions are `z`-free outright,\nand every other position sees `z` only through the product `c₊c₋`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.denom_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.denom_pos","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L153-L155","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cMix_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cMix_pos","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L149-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.vhat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.vhat","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L146-L147","doc":"The corpus vertex readout `V̂ = c₊·μ₊ + c₋·μ₋`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cMix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cMix","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L143-L144","doc":"The mixed (`p`–`n`) eigenfactor `c = (q + q⁻¹)/2`.  It carries no `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cMinus","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L140-L141","doc":"`c₋`, the `λ₋ = -q⁻¹` readout weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.cPlus","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L137-L138","doc":"`c₊`, the `λ₊ = q` readout weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.transferEigen_vieta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.transferEigen_vieta","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L125-L131","doc":"…and the right product, `λ₊ · λ₋ = -1` — the `det S = -1` conjunct of\n`QOU.ParticleInteractions.ground_state_ordering`.  This is the **only**\nconjunct of that proposition that survives; the two ordering conjuncts are\nrefuted by `sorted_lt_prescribed_A5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.transferEigen_isRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GroundStateOrderingRefutation.transferEigen_isRoot","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GroundStateOrderingRefutation.lean#L115-L123","doc":"`q` and `-q⁻¹` are exactly the roots of the characteristic polynomial\n`X² - hX - 1` of the corpus transfer matrix `S = ![![h,1],![1,0]]`, where\n`h = q - q⁻¹`.  This is what collapses `M_i` to `α • 1 + β • S` and hence\ngives the two-term readout `V̂ = c₊μ₊ + c₋μ₋`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}